From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jbevan <jbevan@bu.edu>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 17:23:14 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Server: debug-server test commands on the remote console
 (dbg, MANGBAND_DEBUG_COMMANDS)

A console command "dbg" for automated tests, refused unless the server was started with
MANGBAND_DEBUG_COMMANDS=1 and the console connection is local, so a server without it plays
unchanged. On a logged-in player's level: place a monster (any square, asleep or awake, set HP;
"force" makes a unique that lives elsewhere, is dead or was killed), make an item (kind and ego
by name, the ego that fits the kind; unidentified unless "known"), set terrain (a square or a
rectangle), set the player's state (HP, food, gold, level, timed effects), teleport on the level
or to another depth, clear the level's monsters/objects, and write the level's ground truth as
JSON (players, monsters with HP/sleep/seen, objects with their true kind and ego, the map, what
the player remembers). The full syntax is at the top of src/server/dbgcmd.c.
